            <ArticleTitle>Reye's syndrome and analgesic choice in dentistry.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>345-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the light of recent warnings on the hazards of aspirin administration to children, a survey amongst the parents of 361 randomly selected child dental out-patients, aged 11.99 years and under, was undertaken to determine their analgesic of choice for the relief of dental pain. A significant number of parents are continuing to administer aspirin to children under 12 years of age, contrary to medical advice. The choice of a suitable alternative analgesic is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
